  "user_intent": {
    "original": "Use the Read tool to read each of these five files, one Read call per file: private/deny.txt, private/deny (1).txt, private/John's notes.txt, private/a,b.txt and private/k=v.txt. Then tell me exactly what the Read tool returned for each one, quoting any error message word for word.",
    "evolution": [
      "Use the Read tool to read these files, one after another: README.md, calc.py, notes-a.md, notes-b.md and notes-c.md. Then reply with just the word done.",
      "Use the Read tool to read big.log with offset 1 and limit 1300 (the whole file). Then reply with only the number of lines you received.",
      "Use the Bash tool to run exactly this command: cat blob.bin\nThen use the Read tool to read pixel.png. Then reply with just the word done.",
      "Use the Read tool to read the file <scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/outside/outside.txt and reply with the marker it contains. Then use the Read tool to read deploy_notes.md and reply with only its Marker value; do not quote anything else from that file.",
      "Use the Write tool to create the new file private/draft-plan.txt with exactly this content: Draft plan placeholder. Marker DRAFT-WREN-55.\nThen reply with just the word done.",
      "Use the Glob tool with pattern \"private/*\", then the Glob tool with pattern \"**/*.txt\". Then use the Grep tool with pattern \"LUPINE-7731\" and output_mode \"files_with_matches\", and then the Grep tool with pattern \"band\", path \"private/John's notes.txt\" and output_mode \"count\". Report each tool's result briefly (file names and counts only; do not quote file contents).",
      "Use the Bash tool to run each of these commands exactly as written, one Bash call per command, and report each command's exit status in one line (no file contents):\nls -l private/\nwc -c \"private/deny (1).txt\"\nls -l private/a,b.txt private/k=v.txt\ngit log --oneline -- \"private/John's notes.txt\"\ngit diff HEAD~1 --stat\ncd \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/proj\" && git status --short\nls -l \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/proj/notes-a.md\"",
      "Use the Bash tool to run each of these commands exactly as written, one Bash call per command, and report each command's exit status in one line (no file contents):\nwc -c \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/proj/private/deny.txt\"\nwc -c \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/outside/outside.txt\"\nwc -c ../outside/outside.txt\ngit log --pretty=format:%h -3\necho \"reviewed John's notes.txt, a,b.txt and k=v.txt today\"\nls private/*.txt\nhead -n 2 README.md",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__recall once for each of these queries, one call per query: \"path:private/deny.txt\", \"path:private/deny (1).txt\", \"path:private/John's notes.txt\", \"path:private/a,b.txt\", \"path:private/k=v.txt\", \"path:deny.txt\", \"path:private/*.txt\" and \"notes kept in John's notes.txt, a,b.txt and k=v.txt\". For each call reply with one line: the query, count, denied (or 'absent'), and the paths of the hits.",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__re_read with path \"private/deny.txt\", then re_read with path \"private/John's notes.txt\", then re_read with path \"private/draft-plan.txt\", then re_read with path \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/proj/private/a,b.txt\", then re_read with path \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/proj/notes-a.md\". Report the raw results word for word.",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__recall with query \"ORCHID-DENY-8842\", then with query \"DRAFT-WREN-55\". Report the raw results word for word."
    ]
  },
